(:id "port/luau/vt/text-form" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luautable/vt_text_cells_test.go: TestLuauVtTextCells, TestLuauVtTextCellsNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luautable/json_test.go: TestLuauJsonAgreesWithTheCorpus, TestLuauJsonNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luautable/textdifferential_test.go: TestLuauTextDifferentialAgainstTheGoEngine, TestLuauTextDifferentialNegativeControl") :tested-revision "1af9c231040a7ef597aa210bac8f0fd83a2f1601" :note "2026-11-09: the strict text read (schema_json.luau FromJson) and strict wire read (schema_load.luau ReadStrict) agree with schema-go's own engine on json-read, json-write and json-hostile across fixed-class roots, with artifact-level negative controls. Run on Linux x86-64 at 1af9c231040a7ef597aa210bac8f0fd83a2f1601 under the pinned Luau 0.741 with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1.")
(:id "port/luau/vt/text-form-variable" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luautable/vt_text_cells_test.go: TestLuauVtTextCells, TestLuauVtTextCellsNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luautable/json_test.go: TestLuauJsonAgreesWithTheCorpus, TestLuauJsonNegativeControl") :tested-revision "1af9c231040a7ef597aa210bac8f0fd83a2f1601" :note "2026-11-09: the strict text read (schema_json.luau FromJson) and strict wire read (schema_load.luau ReadStrict) agree with schema-go's own engine on json-read, json-write and json-hostile across variable-class constructs (pointers, &node shared graphs, blobs, string identity, maps, unbounded arrays, 64-bit id-table wire enums, wstring, timestamp, flags, required and optional fields, unions), with artifact-level negative controls. Run on Linux x86-64 at 1af9c231040a7ef597aa210bac8f0fd83a2f1601 under the pinned Luau 0.741 with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1.")
(:id "port/luau/vt/variable-class" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luautable/vt_pointer_cells_test.go: TestLuauVtPointerCells/variable-class" "internal/codegen/luautable/vt_pointer_cells_test.go: TestLuauVtPointerCellsNegativeControl/save-id-count/variable-class, TestLuauVtPointerCellsNegativeControl/load-id-shift/variable-class") :tested-revision "093157f27dd2dc6ee18b3a1df010bebf8e1627b5" :note "2026-11-09: the row's manifest instances load through schema_load's strict read, the whole value or a refusal, and save back byte for byte with measure equal to length; report rows answer reports.txt; a Go-engine construct on the row round-trips when the row has one. The negative controls plant a fault in the emitted Luau and run it. The load plant stores id + integer.create(1) in the variable id table, which the interpreter refuses, and inverts the fixed form-3 check so a good fixed wire is refused. The save plant writes an id-table count one past the entries and writes the fixed form byte as 1. The row goes red under each. The wire-alone refusals node_index_null, node_table_twice, and inert bodies stay with luau-conformance-read-then-write. Run on Linux x86-64 under the pinned Luau 0.741, SCHEMA_SLOW=1 SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1, at this revision.")
